.TH DIR 1.SH NAMEdir \- list a directory.SH SYNOPSIS\fBdir\fR[options] [directory ...].SH DESCRIPTION\fBdir\fRlists the files in each directory named, or in the current one: namesalone, or with\fB\-e\fRthe owner, date last modified, attributes, starting sector and size ofeach.  Dir 1.08, by Lim, changed by Lukas Zeller..SH OPTIONS.TP 12\fB\-a\fRshow every file, including those whose names begin with a dot..TP 12\fB\-e\fRthe extended listing..TP 12\fB\-c\fRshow creation dates..TP 12\fB\-d\fRmark directories with a slash..TP 12\fB\-f\fRshow fragmentation and link counts..TP 12\fB\-h\fRsizes in hexadecimal..TP 12\fB\-k\fRsizes in kilobytes..TP 12\fB\-m\fRsort by date modified..TP 12\fB\-n\fRlist a directory as a file rather than its contents..TP 12\fB\-p\fRlist the directories on the PATH..TP 12\fB\-r\fRrecursive; \fB\-r=\fIn\fR stops at depth\fIn\fR.\fR.TP 12\fB\-s\fRunsorted..SH NOTESNeeds Microware's\fBcio\fR.\fRYour own OS-9 has a\fBdir\fRof its own; see\fBDOC/README-NAMES\fRfor which a bare\fBdir\fRruns..SH SEE ALSOls, du